Kevin the Collector arrived on the 52nd level with bell, book, and candleabrum 
only to discover that he'd forgotten to get candles. Hrumph! A potion of con-
fusion & a scroll of teleportation later he's on the 4th level heading into the
Gnomish mines to get candles from the light shop. Being that a 28th character
has little trouble with the mines (aside from the Wizard popping in
occasionally)
he got the candles applied them to the candleabrum and then went back to hell.
(Interesting that when you try to teleport to lev 52 you go instead to
the gates
 of Gehenna). 
Now when Kevin gets back onto the vibrating square he notices that his book of
the dead is now a book of blank paper! Since I've devoted much time to Kevin
over the last month, I decided to see about wishing for the bloody book. Kevin
went up and visited his favorite temple for a (long) time sacrificing
over a hundred critters. Aside from various other oddments that he
received his luck
became rather high. Now off in search of a throne.... sigh, not a bloody one.

But just as things were getting grim, what does Kevin find in that box over
there? a WoW! Great, now to wish for a 'blessed book of the dead'.... what we
get is a blessed book of blank paper. Tried this with all (six, after
recharging)
wishes, got six blessed blank books. 

The BIG question.... Kevin HAD the book of the dead and it was somehow
'cancelled' or altered (The wizard didn't steal it)...

IS THERE ANYWAY TO GET ANOTHER ONE?!? (or is this game hopeless?)


